WEBVTT

00:00:06.670 --> 00:00:08.020
<i>Surprised?</i>

00:00:08.020 --> 00:00:09.800
<i>I know it's late, but I got you a Christmas present.</i>

00:00:22.330 --> 00:00:23.710
<i>Merry Christmas!</i>

00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:34.360
<i>Joonsang passed away, and so did winter.</i>

00:02:06.660 --> 00:02:07.660
Thanks for your hard work.

00:02:09.040 --> 00:02:10.920
Hey, watch out there!

00:02:11.290 --> 00:02:13.670
Yes, okay.

00:02:13.670 --> 00:02:14.860
Hold on a second, let me get the person in charge.

00:02:16.010 --> 00:02:16.800
Hey!

00:02:17.800 --> 00:02:18.630
Yes?

00:02:19.910 --> 00:02:21.680
Polaris representative Yujin Jung speaking.

00:02:26.270 --> 00:02:27.680
Hold on a second!

00:02:29.520 --> 00:02:30.600
Thank you.

00:02:48.100 --> 00:02:49.500
How's the work coming?

00:02:49.620 --> 00:02:53.080
Seungryong forgot to order the tiles.

00:02:53.250 --> 00:02:56.300
All that construction work today was for nothing.

00:02:59.130 --> 00:03:01.630
I heard today was supposed to be the first snow, but I haven't seen any.

00:03:01.760 --> 00:03:02.780
Other people your age

00:03:02.780 --> 00:03:05.220
don't normally look forward to the first snow, you know.

00:03:11.120 --> 00:03:12.670
Let's turn on the radio.

00:03:12.670 --> 00:03:14.520
I want to listen to "Only You" for some reason.

00:03:14.730 --> 00:03:15.860
The radio?

00:03:15.980 --> 00:03:17.230
Tune it to 93.1.

00:03:17.570 --> 00:03:19.610
Isn't that the classical music channel though?

00:03:23.320 --> 00:03:24.490
What the heck?

00:03:28.540 --> 00:03:30.870
And I thought this was a classical music broadcast.

00:03:31.040 --> 00:03:33.750
Using national radio for private use, are we?

00:03:33.750 --> 00:03:35.670
You sure it's okay to do this, Producer Kim?

00:03:36.290 --> 00:03:38.170
Just this once.

00:03:39.170 --> 00:03:42.090
Fine, but you owe me for this one.

00:03:42.220 --> 00:03:42.660
Sure.

00:03:53.810 --> 00:03:56.810
I'm sure there were quite a few of you who got into arguments

00:03:57.020 --> 00:03:59.820
over whether the sleet that fell a few days ago was the first snow.

00:04:00.230 --> 00:04:02.300
A friend of mine was also waiting for his girlfriend,

00:04:02.420 --> 00:04:04.310
thinking it was the first snow,

00:04:04.310 --> 00:04:05.700
and got into an argument about it instead.

00:04:05.990 --> 00:04:07.890
That first snow better come soon,

00:04:08.010 --> 00:04:10.410
so that lovers like him can finally kiss and make up.

00:04:10.410 --> 00:04:11.500
Why not today?

00:04:16.920 --> 00:04:17.960
Young lady.

00:04:19.220 --> 00:04:19.750
Yes?

00:04:21.380 --> 00:04:22.970
Your man disappeared, didn't he?

00:04:23.530 --> 00:04:24.550
Excuse me?

00:04:24.840 --> 00:04:26.220
I see him.

00:04:26.800 --> 00:04:28.760
You want to find him again, don't you?

00:04:30.100 --> 00:04:31.560
Pardon me?

00:04:32.040 --> 00:04:34.440
I can help you find him again.

00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:38.770
Just give me thirty minutes; I can find him for you.

00:04:38.920 --> 00:04:40.650
He's right here though.

00:04:43.530 --> 00:04:44.490
Thank you.

00:04:45.700 --> 00:04:46.280
When did you arrive?

00:04:46.430 --> 00:04:47.070
A little while ago.

00:04:47.200 --> 00:04:47.740
Did you hear everything?

00:04:47.870 --> 00:04:48.620
Yeah.

00:04:50.240 --> 00:04:53.160
They'll take care of the catering,

00:04:53.160 --> 00:04:54.500
and I already ordered flowers.

00:04:55.750 --> 00:04:56.830
That should be everything, right?

00:04:58.080 --> 00:04:59.200
Think a little harder.

00:04:59.200 --> 00:05:00.210
Haven't you forgotten something?

00:05:02.590 --> 00:05:04.260
I don't think so.

00:05:05.380 --> 00:05:06.630
Really?

00:05:07.020 --> 00:05:08.160
Nope.

00:05:11.100 --> 00:05:12.390
Oh yeah, the rings.

00:05:12.720 --> 00:05:14.390
Do you like them?

00:05:14.600 --> 00:05:16.310
Yeah, they're pretty.

00:05:16.440 --> 00:05:18.360
Why don't we rehearse a little.

00:05:18.360 --> 00:05:19.900
Let me see your hand.

00:05:24.440 --> 00:05:25.320
You too.

00:05:29.450 --> 00:05:32.950
Will you always stay by my side, just like you are right now?

00:05:34.260 --> 00:05:35.210
Yeah.

00:05:36.000 --> 00:05:37.160
Okay.

00:05:39.600 --> 00:05:40.710
Go ahead inside.

00:05:40.840 --> 00:05:42.440
You get going first; it's cold out.

00:05:42.610 --> 00:05:43.630
I'm fine.

00:05:43.630 --> 00:05:44.510
Go ahead.

00:05:49.950 --> 00:05:50.930
Drive safe!

00:05:51.470 --> 00:05:53.060
I'll call you when I get home.

00:05:53.680 --> 00:05:55.520
Sweet dreams; good night.

00:05:55.640 --> 00:05:57.180
You too.

00:06:02.900 --> 00:06:04.130
Let's hurry it up.

00:06:04.130 --> 00:06:05.230
It's almost time.

00:06:05.360 --> 00:06:06.690
I'm almost done.

00:06:06.800 --> 00:06:09.430
Isn't MARCIAN asking for a little too much?

00:06:10.360 --> 00:06:12.270
They're under new management, aren't they?

00:06:12.270 --> 00:06:14.200
These things always get a little complicated with new management.

00:06:14.310 --> 00:06:15.800
What kind of a person is he?

00:06:15.800 --> 00:06:18.080
Is he some sort of a salesman who has no business in construction?

00:06:18.210 --> 00:06:19.770
He had an impressive track record though;

00:06:19.770 --> 00:06:21.900
apparently he was the one who designed

00:06:21.900 --> 00:06:23.460
Whitney Resort and Saint Museum.

00:06:24.460 --> 00:06:28.760
He's also nabbed himself the Pritzker Prize that I've been gunning for.

00:06:28.880 --> 00:06:31.910
Why doesn't he just go solo then?

00:06:31.910 --> 00:06:32.890
He shouldn't be working for a company.

00:06:33.010 --> 00:06:34.580
Apparently he's either a cousin or an heir

00:06:34.580 --> 00:06:36.350
to the resort company he was working with or something.

00:06:36.470 --> 00:06:38.440
He's got skills and a good background...

00:06:38.440 --> 00:06:40.230
now all he needs is a good looking face.

00:06:40.390 --> 00:06:41.930
Was he handsome, Yujin?

00:06:41.930 --> 00:06:43.360
Was he married or not?

00:06:43.900 --> 00:06:45.320
How should I know?

00:06:45.320 --> 00:06:47.070
I haven't even met him.

00:06:47.570 --> 00:06:50.240
But you've been over there so many times already.

00:06:50.490 --> 00:06:51.910
Is he better looking than I am?

00:06:52.410 --> 00:06:53.820
I'm done.

00:06:54.050 --> 00:06:55.660
You could at least answer me.

00:06:55.790 --> 00:06:57.620
Just go deliver it, will you?

00:06:58.370 --> 00:07:00.870
I'll clock out early and deliver it on my way home.

00:07:01.580 --> 00:07:02.920
It's okay, I'll do it.

00:07:03.460 --> 00:07:05.130
Do you have something to do today?

00:07:05.920 --> 00:07:08.010
Today's my engagement party.

00:07:08.670 --> 00:07:09.340
What?!

00:07:18.390 --> 00:07:19.730
I'm sorry.

00:07:22.850 --> 00:07:23.900
Deputy Manager Kim.

00:07:24.020 --> 00:07:25.990
I'm sorry it's a bit of a mess in here;

00:07:25.990 --> 00:07:27.530
we're setting up the director's room.

00:07:27.650 --> 00:07:29.990
Oh, the newcomer, right?

00:07:30.110 --> 00:07:32.960
Our other associates are all going crazy because of the new director.

00:07:32.960 --> 00:07:34.190
What about you guys at Polaris?

00:07:34.190 --> 00:07:34.950
Has he been strict with you too?

00:07:35.070 --> 00:07:36.450
He made us redraw this five times.

00:07:36.530 --> 00:07:38.950
At least he didn't reject you guys flat out.

00:07:39.080 --> 00:07:41.250
But then again, the director was the one who contacted you.

00:07:41.250 --> 00:07:43.460
He said that you guys at least "won't get lost" or something like that.

00:07:44.960 --> 00:07:46.290
You can give that to me since he's not around.

00:07:46.510 --> 00:07:47.420
Okay.

00:07:48.550 --> 00:07:50.250
Oh, hold on a second there.

00:07:50.250 --> 00:07:51.880
This puzzle goes in the director's room.

00:07:52.720 --> 00:07:55.090
I don't get why he bothers with this.

00:07:55.090 --> 00:07:56.970
What does he get out of this thing? He's not a kid.

00:07:57.220 --> 00:07:58.930
Maybe he's really bored,

00:07:59.220 --> 00:08:02.770
or maybe he has things he wants to remember piece-by-piece.

00:08:03.980 --> 00:08:05.600
He must have been bored then.

00:08:06.190 --> 00:08:06.940
You should be going.

00:08:07.480 --> 00:08:08.940
Thank you.

00:08:30.130 --> 00:08:32.590
Father said he's on his way from school already.

00:08:32.840 --> 00:08:33.670
Really?

00:08:33.950 --> 00:08:36.470
And Yujin's getting her hair done at the salon.

00:08:36.970 --> 00:08:40.660
Remember, I only agreed to accept her as my daughter-in-law

00:08:40.660 --> 00:08:42.560
because <i>you</i> like her, okay?

00:08:43.620 --> 00:08:45.640
She'll be a good daughter-in-law, I promise.

00:08:46.290 --> 00:08:47.740
I wasn't implying that she wasn't.

00:08:47.740 --> 00:08:49.440
I just wanted to remind you, that's all.

00:08:51.150 --> 00:08:53.490
You have such nice hair.

00:08:54.530 --> 00:08:56.570
You look so beautiful!

00:08:56.950 --> 00:08:58.620
Many congratulations.

00:08:58.960 --> 00:08:59.950
Thank you.

00:09:00.660 --> 00:09:03.370
Thank you so much for coming today.

00:09:03.500 --> 00:09:04.250
Mother.

00:09:05.330 --> 00:09:07.170
Yujin's mother is here.

00:09:08.750 --> 00:09:09.670
How are you?

00:09:09.790 --> 00:09:13.010
Welcome. It must have been a hassle to come this far.

00:09:13.590 --> 00:09:15.050
Oh, no.

00:09:15.470 --> 00:09:18.640
Your face looks so much better, Mrs. Jung.

00:09:19.930 --> 00:09:22.230
'Mrs. Jung' is no way to address her;

00:09:22.230 --> 00:09:24.310
you should call her by her first name.

00:09:24.430 --> 00:09:26.440
We're family now, right?

00:09:27.170 --> 00:09:28.480
You're right.

00:09:28.600 --> 00:09:30.230
Yes, my apologies.

00:09:31.070 --> 00:09:33.500
I'll be right there.

00:09:37.340 --> 00:09:38.410
It's snowing!

00:09:40.320 --> 00:09:42.240
This is the first snow, isn't it?

00:09:41.100 --> 00:09:42.080
Hey, it's Daddy.

00:09:42.080 --> 00:09:44.190
Yeah, it's snowing outside.

00:09:45.830 --> 00:09:48.170
I'll buy some cake on my way in, okay?

00:10:14.750 --> 00:10:16.280
<i>J-Joonsang...</i>

00:10:26.720 --> 00:10:27.790
Joonsang!

00:10:31.500 --> 00:10:33.880
Please, come in.

00:10:34.380 --> 00:10:36.000
Congratulations.

00:10:36.000 --> 00:10:36.420
Why, thank you.

00:10:36.420 --> 00:10:37.970
You look so handsome tonight.

00:10:38.090 --> 00:10:38.720
Hey, Sanghyuk.

00:10:38.880 --> 00:10:41.680
Would you wipe that smirk off your face already?

00:10:41.800 --> 00:10:42.760
He's right.

00:10:42.970 --> 00:10:43.930
Are you really <i>that</i> happy?

00:10:46.850 --> 00:10:48.300
Cut me some slack.

00:10:48.300 --> 00:10:49.430
Did Yujin leave the salon yet?

00:10:49.600 --> 00:10:51.600
Yeah, she said she'd be here soon.

00:10:52.310 --> 00:10:56.610
Ever since we were in school, she's always been late, hasn't she?

00:10:56.730 --> 00:10:58.650
She still has twenty minutes, you know.

00:11:10.660 --> 00:11:11.790
Joonsang...

00:11:13.000 --> 00:11:14.630
What's taking her so long?

00:11:14.790 --> 00:11:16.380
Why isn't she here?

00:11:30.930 --> 00:11:31.850
Joonsang...

00:11:36.270 --> 00:11:37.110
Joonsang.

00:12:03.930 --> 00:12:04.970
<i>Joonsang.</i>

00:12:22.190 --> 00:12:22.990
Yujin.

00:12:36.230 --> 00:12:39.090
I'm so sorry about this.

00:12:39.090 --> 00:12:40.000
I'll contact you later.

00:12:42.260 --> 00:12:43.170
Oh Yujin...

00:12:43.730 --> 00:12:45.240
You shouldn't worry yourself so much.

00:12:45.240 --> 00:12:46.640
I'm sure she's fine.

00:12:47.220 --> 00:12:51.100
Yes, let's calm down and give her a little more time.

00:12:52.270 --> 00:12:53.100
Oh, Sanghyuk.

00:12:53.230 --> 00:12:53.810
Father.

00:12:53.930 --> 00:12:56.190
So, what did the police say?

00:12:57.150 --> 00:12:58.980
They haven't had any reports come in.

00:13:00.690 --> 00:13:03.570
I think I should go look for her.

00:13:03.690 --> 00:13:04.820
Let's give her a little more time.

00:13:04.950 --> 00:13:06.110
Yeah, Sanghyuk.

00:13:08.660 --> 00:13:09.410
Yujin!

00:13:10.490 --> 00:13:10.990
Yujin!

00:13:11.160 --> 00:13:12.950
Where have you been?

00:13:13.250 --> 00:13:14.450
What happened?

00:13:15.270 --> 00:13:16.670
Yujin!

00:13:17.170 --> 00:13:20.790
What's going on, tell me!

00:13:21.000 --> 00:13:23.840
I don't really know either.

00:13:23.960 --> 00:13:25.420
Oh, Yujin...

00:13:27.430 --> 00:13:29.970
Looks like we were worried for nothing.

00:13:30.260 --> 00:13:31.510
I'm going to head back first.

00:13:33.600 --> 00:13:34.430
M-Mother!

00:13:34.640 --> 00:13:35.560
Mrs. Kim—

00:13:36.600 --> 00:13:38.690
What in the world happened, Yujin?

00:13:39.980 --> 00:13:41.980
Don't you have something to say for yourself?

00:13:42.360 --> 00:13:45.610
How could you be late to our engagement party?

00:13:45.760 --> 00:13:46.820
Sanghyuk,

00:13:47.420 --> 00:13:48.490
I...

00:13:50.530 --> 00:13:51.320
Yujin!

00:13:51.530 --> 00:13:52.820
Yujin!

00:13:52.820 --> 00:13:53.950
Get a hold of yourself!

00:13:53.670 --> 00:13:55.210
What's going on?

00:13:54.080 --> 00:13:57.210
<i>I saw Joonsang...</i>

00:13:55.210 --> 00:13:56.540
What's wrong with her?

00:13:57.310 --> 00:13:58.920
Wake up, Yujin!

00:14:13.100 --> 00:14:14.890
Sanghyuk just left a few moments ago.

00:14:16.290 --> 00:14:17.480
What's going on?

00:14:18.270 --> 00:14:19.980
Tell me, what is it?

00:14:23.610 --> 00:14:25.780
Is it something you can't tell your own mother?

00:14:31.450 --> 00:14:35.080
Are things not going well with Sanghyuk?

00:14:35.450 --> 00:14:36.540
Is that what it is?

00:14:39.370 --> 00:14:40.580
Lighten up.

00:14:40.580 --> 00:14:41.500
I'm sure there was a reason for it.

00:14:46.420 --> 00:14:47.950
Drink slowly.

00:14:47.950 --> 00:14:48.800
Otherwise you'll get drunk.

00:14:49.260 --> 00:14:50.460
I'm fine.

00:14:50.460 --> 00:14:52.800
A little too fine, actually.

00:14:53.430 --> 00:14:54.550
What did Yujin say?

00:14:59.730 --> 00:15:00.870
When we were about eight,

00:15:00.870 --> 00:15:03.520
we got our hair cut together at the neighborhood salon.

00:15:03.860 --> 00:15:05.870
You know how everyone used to get bob cuts back then, right?

00:15:05.870 --> 00:15:08.840
The neighborhood ladies teased us when we left with the same hairstyle.

00:15:08.840 --> 00:15:10.200
They'd ask us if we were twins.

00:15:10.340 --> 00:15:12.700
Do you know what Yujin told them, back then?

00:15:13.280 --> 00:15:16.950
"Other than both being eight years old, we're nothing alike!"

00:15:17.830 --> 00:15:18.410
Did she really?

00:15:18.520 --> 00:15:20.850
And then we said that we weren't twins,

00:15:20.850 --> 00:15:22.710
but future husband and wife.

00:15:23.060 --> 00:15:23.920
Yujin said that?

00:15:24.020 --> 00:15:25.040
No, I did.

00:15:27.000 --> 00:15:28.670
Anyway, how's Yujin doing?

00:15:29.590 --> 00:15:30.880
She said she saw Joonsang.

00:15:31.630 --> 00:15:32.720
W-What?

00:15:33.200 --> 00:15:34.570
I know it can't be him,

00:15:34.570 --> 00:15:37.810
but hearing her say that name makes me a little uneasy.

00:15:40.100 --> 00:15:43.850
I wonder how things would have turned out now

00:15:45.400 --> 00:15:47.570
if I had been the one to find her when she was lost in the mountains.

00:15:54.360 --> 00:15:56.370
Please don't be like this, Mother.

00:15:56.490 --> 00:15:58.540
I'm not in the mood to talk.

00:15:58.660 --> 00:16:01.960
Could you please come out of the room and talk?

00:16:02.120 --> 00:16:03.040
Sanghyuk.

00:16:03.890 --> 00:16:06.040
Why don't you stop trying for today and come sit down.

00:16:06.460 --> 00:16:07.340
But Father—

00:16:07.460 --> 00:16:08.750
That's enough for one day.

00:16:09.250 --> 00:16:13.300
You'll only make it harder for Yujin if you keep trying.

00:16:14.800 --> 00:16:16.010
You're going home, right?

00:16:17.350 --> 00:16:19.350
Sanghyuk, I...

00:16:20.010 --> 00:16:21.900
I'm not angry about yesterday.

00:16:21.900 --> 00:16:23.210
Not having an engagement party

00:16:23.210 --> 00:16:24.890
isn't going to change anything, after all.

00:16:27.650 --> 00:16:29.400
Come on, I'll drive you home.

00:16:29.770 --> 00:16:31.860
It's okay, I'll go by myself.

00:16:31.940 --> 00:16:33.110
I'll take you.

00:16:33.950 --> 00:16:36.270
You should go inside and console your mother.

00:16:36.270 --> 00:16:38.620
I'm sure she's very disappointed because of me.

00:16:40.080 --> 00:16:41.020
Okay.

00:16:41.020 --> 00:16:42.100
I'll call you.

00:16:42.100 --> 00:16:42.910
Take care.

00:16:59.260 --> 00:17:01.930
<i>Was seeing you just a dream?</i>

00:17:03.180 --> 00:17:06.810
<i>I still remember so much.</i>

00:17:07.850 --> 00:17:10.190
<i>I remember the sound of the piano you played for me,</i>

00:17:10.770 --> 00:17:14.190
<i>the lakeside sunset that we walked in together,</i>

00:17:15.170 --> 00:17:20.030
<i>and the smile that came to my face when you held my hand;</i>

00:17:20.830 --> 00:17:22.450
<i>I still remember them all.</i>

00:17:23.850 --> 00:17:25.500
<i>I always prayed,</i>

00:17:26.660 --> 00:17:28.560
<i>that one day I might,</i>

00:17:28.560 --> 00:17:31.170
<i>once again, be able to see your smile that lives in my memories.</i>

00:17:32.860 --> 00:17:36.260
<i>Did the first snow grant me my wish?</i>

00:17:37.510 --> 00:17:43.430
<i>Or was it just me dreaming amidst the first snow that day?</i>

00:17:45.100 --> 00:17:48.900
<i>Where are you now, Joonsang?</i>

00:17:49.940 --> 00:17:53.150
<i>Where are you?</i>

00:17:56.070 --> 00:17:57.360
<i>Long time no see.</i>

00:17:57.360 --> 00:17:58.530
<i>It's me, Chelin.</i>

00:17:58.660 --> 00:18:01.240
<i>I hope you haven't forgotten who I am.</i>

00:18:02.680 --> 00:18:05.260
<i>I know what you two have been up to,</i>

00:18:05.260 --> 00:18:07.830
<i>but I figured I'd fill you guys in with some of my recent news.</i>

00:18:08.290 --> 00:18:09.430
<i>Don't forget to get your hopes up high;</i>

00:18:09.430 --> 00:18:12.750
<i>there will be a surprise waiting for you guys pretty soon.</i>

00:18:13.210 --> 00:18:15.260
I guess miracles do happen;

00:18:15.260 --> 00:18:17.840
I never thought Chelin would ever contact us.

00:18:17.970 --> 00:18:19.140
She must have been lonely or something.

00:18:19.140 --> 00:18:20.430
She <i>has</i> been abroad for seven years, you know.

00:18:20.680 --> 00:18:22.760
What do you think she means by "surprise"?

00:18:23.050 --> 00:18:24.600
Maybe she bagged herself a French guy or something.

00:18:24.760 --> 00:18:26.020
No way.

00:18:26.470 --> 00:18:28.810
Chelin's not the type who'd worry about nationality when it comes to love.

00:18:29.270 --> 00:18:30.810
You should learn that from her.

00:18:31.230 --> 00:18:33.860
You'd think you'd at least have had one boyfriend at your age.

00:18:34.400 --> 00:18:35.530
What about you?

00:18:35.860 --> 00:18:37.510
I'm taking a breather.

00:18:37.510 --> 00:18:40.360
I've had too many runs under my belt.

00:18:40.530 --> 00:18:41.990
Why don't you just keep running.

00:18:46.390 --> 00:18:47.950
How's Yujin though?

00:18:48.750 --> 00:18:50.230
She's still the way she was.

00:18:50.870 --> 00:18:52.980
This is frustrating.

00:18:52.980 --> 00:18:55.170
I wish there was something I could do for her, as a friend.

00:18:56.300 --> 00:18:57.260
Yeah.

00:18:59.130 --> 00:19:03.090
If only her engagement party had gone well...

00:19:03.550 --> 00:19:04.890
That's it, the engagement party!

00:19:05.140 --> 00:19:07.560
That's why they're in this mess right now, you know.

00:19:07.720 --> 00:19:08.850
That's what I'm saying.

00:19:08.850 --> 00:19:12.310
To fix a big problem you need to start by undoing the knots, right?

00:19:13.980 --> 00:19:15.480
Where are we going?

00:19:15.630 --> 00:19:16.570
Somewhere nice.

00:19:17.020 --> 00:19:17.980
And where's that?

00:19:18.090 --> 00:19:18.990
It's a secret.

00:19:19.820 --> 00:19:21.360
It'd be no fun if I told you.

00:19:21.900 --> 00:19:24.160
I was in the middle of doing laundry though.

00:19:26.490 --> 00:19:28.620
Laundry can wait.

00:19:48.600 --> 00:19:50.810
<i>This</i> is where you wanted to bring me?

00:19:52.100 --> 00:19:54.290
Hurry up will you, Captain Tardy?

00:19:54.940 --> 00:19:55.900
Why you...

00:20:01.320 --> 00:20:02.950
It's been a while since we were last here, huh?

00:20:03.070 --> 00:20:03.570
Yeah.

00:20:04.610 --> 00:20:07.300
They should be here any minute now.

00:20:09.450 --> 00:20:10.700
They're here.

00:20:11.250 --> 00:20:11.730
Yongguk!

00:20:11.810 --> 00:20:12.580
Yongguk!

00:20:14.750 --> 00:20:15.830
Okay.

00:20:21.130 --> 00:20:22.630
It hasn't changed a bit, huh?

00:20:22.760 --> 00:20:23.750
Yeah.

00:20:24.260 --> 00:20:25.340
You're right.

00:20:27.600 --> 00:20:28.450
<i>Can you hear me?</i>

00:20:30.640 --> 00:20:33.350
<i>Back by popular demand,</i>

00:20:33.850 --> 00:20:36.940
<i>this is DJ Yongguk, after ten year's hiatus.</i>

00:20:38.480 --> 00:20:40.690
<i>And what kind of a day is today, you ask?</i>

00:20:41.150 --> 00:20:43.920
<i>Today's the day when we redo</i>

00:20:44.170 --> 00:20:47.620
<i>Sanghyuk and Yujin's engagement party.</i>

00:20:48.200 --> 00:20:51.330
<i>Now you two, face each other.</i>

00:20:53.200 --> 00:20:54.710
<i>Why am I getting nervous?</i>

00:20:55.330 --> 00:20:58.040
<i>Now Sanghyuk, give her the thing you prepared.</i>

00:21:11.890 --> 00:21:13.910
You have no idea how happy and thankful I am

00:21:13.910 --> 00:21:16.810
that you're standing in front of me now.

00:21:17.600 --> 00:21:20.060
Don't forget that I'll always be by your side.

00:21:24.860 --> 00:21:26.700
<i>That's a nice atmosphere you guys got going.</i>

00:21:27.150 --> 00:21:29.860
<i>How dare you two blemish these holy school grounds with your love.</i>

00:21:31.030 --> 00:21:32.780
<i>Since we've come this far, let's go all the way.</i>

00:21:32.780 --> 00:21:34.160
<i>Show us a kiss!</i>

00:21:34.520 --> 00:21:35.850
<i>Kiss!</i>

00:21:36.350 --> 00:21:37.390
Thanks for the sentiment,

00:21:37.390 --> 00:21:39.250
but it sounds to me like you guys are the ones who want to do it.

00:21:39.380 --> 00:21:42.550
<i>Long time no see, Yujin and Sanghyuk.</i>

00:21:43.380 --> 00:21:45.220
<i>You guys are getting married now?</i>

00:21:45.220 --> 00:21:46.950
<i>I'm impressed.</i>

00:21:46.950 --> 00:21:48.380
<i>Don't you guys ever get sick of each other?</i>

00:21:49.970 --> 00:21:50.530
Is that Chelin?

00:21:59.730 --> 00:22:01.310
Congratulations on your engagement!

00:22:01.310 --> 00:22:01.770
Thanks.

00:22:01.790 --> 00:22:03.440
Congratulations, Yujin.

00:22:06.780 --> 00:22:07.820
Chelin.

00:22:08.490 --> 00:22:11.060
You really haven't changed, have you?

00:22:11.060 --> 00:22:12.280
You still have that same old lame bob cut.

00:22:12.410 --> 00:22:13.080
What?

00:22:13.530 --> 00:22:14.330
I'm just kidding.

00:22:14.450 --> 00:22:17.410
And now, 1, 2, 3!

00:22:19.100 --> 00:22:19.870
Congratulations!

00:22:20.250 --> 00:22:21.210
Thanks.

00:22:21.630 --> 00:22:23.380
When did you open your boutique shop?

00:22:23.840 --> 00:22:25.130
Last week;

00:22:25.130 --> 00:22:27.010
I would have contacted you guys sooner if I hadn't been so busy.

00:22:27.090 --> 00:22:28.670
You don't sell guys clothes, do you?

00:22:29.010 --> 00:22:31.950
We do, but our clothes are a little too expensive

00:22:31.950 --> 00:22:33.220
for you to be buying them out of friendship.

00:22:33.300 --> 00:22:35.290
More like, your sense in fashion

00:22:35.290 --> 00:22:38.020
is a little too peculiar for me to be wearing them out of friendship.

00:22:38.180 --> 00:22:38.890
What?

00:22:39.120 --> 00:22:41.560
Would you two cut it out?

00:22:41.690 --> 00:22:43.900
Why don't we listen to some music?

00:22:46.730 --> 00:22:47.990
What's taking him so long?

00:22:48.740 --> 00:22:49.490
What is?

00:22:50.610 --> 00:22:51.610
Oh nothing.

00:22:52.110 --> 00:22:53.980
"The First Time"?

00:22:53.980 --> 00:22:55.160
This thing's still here?

00:22:57.160 --> 00:22:59.910
You used to listen to this like everyday before graduation.

00:23:00.580 --> 00:23:02.040
Why don't we listen to something else?

00:23:02.150 --> 00:23:04.420
But you like this song, don't you?

00:23:19.700 --> 00:23:20.520
Who could that be?

00:23:20.980 --> 00:23:21.790
No clue.

00:23:26.100 --> 00:23:26.860
Hey...
